stereo-layer (1.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Picture::load() and Picture::loadPair() read a depthSeparate picture's
    depth map as the reader's second image (the edition's KImageFormats gives
    HEIF and AVIF depth items, Dynamic Depth, GDepth and Apple's portrait
    photos so) and draw its views; new overloads take the user's DepthOptions
    and the picture the views are drawn from (as shown, or the original
    before the camera's effects, a reader's third image).
  * Depth marks 0.2 (docs/depth-marks.md): how readers give the images, and
    the phones' formats: Apple's depth description first, Dynamic Depth,
    GDepth, and the auxiliary images that are no depth.
  * libstereo-layer1 depends on kimageformat6-plugins 6.30.0-1+stereo3d3,
    the readers that give pictures with their depth map.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:45:29 -0300

stereo-layer (1.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depth marks (docs/depth-marks.md, version 0.1): the depth layouts of
    Stereo3DLayout (a picture and its depth side by side or top and bottom
    either way, HDMI 1.4a's four rows with graphics, four quarters with the
    background, or the depth map on its own) and Stereo3DDepth, what a depth
    sample means, each tied to its source.
  * libstereo-policy reads the depth layouts; libstereo-layer draws marked
    pictures (Picture::fromDepth(), Stereo::DepthOptions).
  * libstereo-dibr: Dynamic Depth's RangeLinear and RangeInverse, depth
    sensors' distances with 0 for no measurement, DepthLUT (H.265 equation
    G-10), the Stereo3DDepth mark read and written in any locale, a second
    layer (the background a picture hides, or graphics over it), and the
    whole DIBR core as GLSL passes run in the caller's OpenGL 3.3 or OpenGL
    ES 3.0 context (stereo-dibr-gl.h; the shaders in
    /usr/share/stereo-dibr/glsl), tested against the C code.
  * The sources formatted as .clang-format asks, so the CI's format job
    passes.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:08:16 -0300

stereo-layer (1.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New library libstereo-dibr (packages libstereo-dibr1 and
    libstereo-dibr-dev): depth-image-based rendering without Qt. A picture
    and its depth map become the two views of full side by side, from the
    depth conventions of H.265 Table G.3 and H.264 Table H-1, the parallax
    map of ISO/IEC 23002-3 as we read it (unverified) and 2D-plus-depth;
    the picture as the left eye or the middle; forward, backward or layered
    warping; background extension, depth-aided, Telea or no hole filling;
    the depth smoothed by an asymmetric Gaussian or not. FFmpeg's dibr
    filter is built on it.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:41:50 -0300

stereo-layer (1.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Picture::load() and Picture::loadPair() compare the halves of an unmarked
    picture with the file decoded at the width of the comparison, apart from
    the decode that is shown, so a thumbnail, a larger preview and a viewer
    give the same answer: before, a picture near the thresholds could be flat
    in its thumbnail and 3D in a larger preview, or the other way round.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:00:00 -0300

stereo-layer (1.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libstereo-policy: one rule for every video player. The user's explicit
    choice of a packing, or STEREO_POLICY_USER_FORCE_2D (not 3D), comes before
    the stream's mark; swap eyes still reverses what was decided.
  * stereo_policy_video_views() tells full from half views by what the stream
    says: Matroska's one-plane display size (RFC 9559 section 18.10) and the
    H.265 upsampled_aspect_ratio_flag (D.3.16), then by shape.
    stereo_policy_matroska_plane() and Stereo::Video::matroskaPlane() undo
    the folding of the plane size into the sample aspect ratio by FFmpeg.
  * The shape rule is named: a single picture is 5:4 to 12:5
    (STEREO_POLICY_SINGLE_PICTURE_*), so a marked frame of that shape holds
    half views and a doubled one full views. The private 2.5 and 1.2 limits
    are gone.
  * stereo_policy_name_tag() and stereo_policy_video_layout_named() read the
    3D tag of a file name (3D, SBS, TAB, OU and their half and full forms,
    LR, RL) after the user's choice and the stream's marks and before the
    shape. stereo_policy_halves_test() compares the halves of a decoded frame
    for a bare 3D tag. Stereo::Video gets nameTag().
  * The 1.4 signatures and symbols stay.
  * Carries the anaglyph detector fix of the picture lane: both colour sides
    of the pair are required, so a red-on-grey 2D picture no longer counts as
    an anaglyph. The H.264 frame packing table is cited as D-8 in V15 and D-9
    in V16.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:40:00 -0300

